{title: Until a Priest Should Arise}
{subtitle: Ezra 2:61–63; 2:62; 2:63; Nehemiah 7:63–65}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [F] | [Bb] | [Eb] [F] |
| [Gm] | [Eb] [F] | [Gm] [Dm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]We came from exile to the [F/A]city [Bb]gate
With [Eb]Zerubba[F]bel and the faithful [Bb]band
[Eb]Seeking our [F]place in the [Gm]holy es[Eb]tate
But the [Cm7]records of our names were [F]scant
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Sons of Hobaiah and [F/A]Hakkoz [Bb]too
And [Eb]Barzillai who [F]took the Gileadite [Bb]name
We [Eb]sought the en[F]try in the [Gm]book a[Eb]new
But [Cm7]the trace was lost [F]in history's [Bb]flame
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]They searched for our [F]name in the [Bb]registers
[Eb]But it could not be [F]found by the [Gm]eye
Ex[Eb]cluded from the priest[F]hood as un[Gm]clean [Gm7/F]we [Eb]stand
De[Cm7]nied the holy service to re[F]ly
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]The governor [F]spoke with a [Bb]firm decree
[Eb]Do not [F]eat of the most [Gm]holy food
[Eb]Until a priest [F]should arise in [Gm]the day
To consult [Eb]the Urim and Thummim in the [F]cloud
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]We [F]wait for the [Eb]sign [F]that we are [Bb][Eb][F]clean [Bb]
{end_of_verse}
